SUMMARY:Embedded Counseling (CAPS)
DESCRIPTION:Supporting your well-being is an important part of our work a
 t the LGBTQ+ Culture Center. That's why we are proud to partner with Coun
 seling &amp\; Psychological Services (CAPS) to provide an embedded counse
 lor in our space every Monday from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.  Mollibeth Penn
 er\, LHMCA serves as our embedded counselor and works directly with stude
 nts connected to the LGBTQ+ Culture Center. To schedule an appointment\, 
 please call CAPS (https://healthcenter.indiana.edu/make-appointment/index
 .html) and let them know you are an LGBTQ+ Culture Center student interes
 ted in meeting with Mollibeth at the center.      We hope this partnershi
 p makes it easier for you to access support in a space where you feel com
 fortable and affirmed.  All Indiana University events\, groups\, activiti
 es\, educational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome all memb
 ers of the Indiana University community.
