 e Heard!</strong></p><p>                                  Join us for an 
 evening of conversation\, learning\, and community as we explore the powe
 r of voting and civic engagement in shaping a more inclusive future for L
 GBTQ+ communities. Our guest speaker\, Professor Steve Sanders\, will sha
 re insights on the history of voting rights\, the impact of collective ac
 tion\, and why participation in the 2026 election matters. Whether you're
  a first-time voter or a longtime advocate\, you'll have the opportunity 
 to ask questions\, share perspectives\, and connect with others who are p
 assionate about making a difference.                                </p><
 p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">Steve Sanders is Associate Dea
 n for Academic Affairs and Professor of Law in the Maurer School of Law a
 t IU Bloomington. He holds additional appointments as an Adjunct Professo
 r of Political Science and an affiliated faculty member with the Departme
 nt of Gender Studies and the Kinsey Institute. Steve's primary teaching a
 rea is Constitutional Law\, and his scholarship focuses on questions aris
 ing out of the Fourteenth Amendment's guarantees of equal protection and 
 due process\, with a special focus on issues affecting LGBTQ persons and 
 same-sex couples. Steve developed and taught IU's first course on "Gay an
 d Lesbian Politics" in 1996\, chaired the committee that won approval for
  domestic partner benefits in 2001\, and was a longtime member of the boa
 rd of the IU LGBTQ+ Alumni Association. He has received a Leadership Awar
 d from Lambda Legal and is a three-time winner of the IU Trustees Teachin
 g Award.</span></p><p><strong>Ready to take action? Register to vote!</st
 rong> Visit <strong>www.indianavoters.in.gov</strong> to check your regis
 tration status or register to vote (you can also click on the "register" 
 button below). Follow the LGBTQ+ Culture Center on <strong>QNews\, Facebo
 ok\, and Instagram</strong> for voter registration updates\, election inf
 ormation\, and important deadlines. <strong>The deadline to register to v
 ote in Indiana is October 5\, 2026.</strong></p><p>                      
             Come learn\, connect\, and take the next step toward making y
 our voice count.                                </p><p><strong>All Indian
 a University events\, groups\, activities\, educational\, cultural\, and 
 historical observances welcome all members of the Indiana University comm
 unity.</strong></p><p>                                  &#160\;          
